            <ArticleTitle>Vitamin E supplements and coronary heart disease.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>333-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Although two new epidemiologic studies on the association between vitamin E and heart disease do not resolve important issues related to dose-response, mechanisms of action, or specificity, they do provide important evidence that supports the development of new strategies for preventing heart disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
